final_output:  ["547,289. Wait a second, let me double-check that to make sure I didn't mix up any digits. Let me add them again using another method to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, adding the numbers:\n\n322,313\n+224,976\n=?\n\nLet me add the numbers step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 3 + 6 = 9 ✔️\n\nTens: 1 + 7 = 8 ✔️\n\nHundreds: 3 + 9 = 12. So 2, carryover 1. ✔️\n\nThousands: 2 (from first number) +4 (second) +1 (carry) =7 ✔️\n\nTen thousands: 2 +2 =4 ✔️\n\nHundred thousands: 3 +2=5 ✔️\n\nYes, that gives 547,289. Wait, but when I write the digits in order: hundred thousands (5), ten thousands (4), thousands (7), hundreds (2), tens (8), ones (9). So 547,289. That seems right. Hmm, but let me do the addition another way to verify.\n\nAlternatively, adding 322,313 + 224,976:\n\nMaybe break them into parts:\n\n322,313 + 200,000 = 522,313\n\n522,313 + 24,000 = 546,313\n\n546,313 + 976 = 547,289. Yep, same result. Okay, that checks out. So I think the answer is correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 322,313 and 224,976 is \\boxed{547289}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 322313 and 224976?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: \\(3 + 6 = 9\\)\n2. The tens place: \\(1 + 7 = 8\\)\n3. The hundreds place: \\(3 + 9 = 12\\). Write down 2 and carry over 1.\n4. The thousands place: \\(2 + 4 + 1 = 7\\)\n5. The ten thousands place: \\(2 + 2 = 4\\)\n6. The hundred thousands place: \\(3 + 2 = 5\\)\n\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is \\boxed{547289}.", '']
