3. Write 3, carry 1.\n\nTens place: 7 + 9 = 16, plus 1 is 17. Write 7, carry 1.\n\nHundreds place: 6 + 9 = 15, plus 1 is 16. Write 6, carry 1.\n\nThousands place: 4 (from first number) + 1 (from second number) = 5, plus 1 carried over makes 6. So 6 here, no carry.\n\nTen thousands place: 4 (from first number) + 2 (from second number) = 6. No carryover.\n\nHundred thousands place: 7 + 7 = 14. So write 4 and carry over 1, but since there are no more digits, that 1 becomes a new digit at the beginning.\n\nPutting it all together: The digits from right to left are 3,7,6,6,6,4,1? Wait, let me check again.\n\nWait, let me go step by step again carefully.\n\nLet me list each digit position:.\n\nStarting from the right (ones):.\n\n1. Ones place:.\n   - 5 (from 744675) + 8 (from 721998) = 13.\n   - Write 3, carryover 1.\n\n2. Tens place:.\n   - 7 + 9 = 16, plus 1 carried over = 17.\n   - Write 7, carryover 1.\n\n3. Hundreds place:.\n   - 6 + 9 = 15, plus 1 = 16.\n   - Write 6, carryover 1.\n\n4. Thousands place:.\n   - 4 (from first number) + 1 (from second number) = 5, plus 1 = 6.\n   - Write 6, no carryover.\n\n5. Ten thousands place:.\n   - 4 (first number) + 2 (second number) = 6.\n   - Write 6, no carryover.\n\n6. Hundred thousands place:.\n   - 7 + 7 = 14.\n   - Write 4 and carryover 1. But since there are no more digits, add the 1 in front.\n\nSo putting all the digits together from right to left:.\n\nThe digits we wrote are:.\n\nOnes: 3.\n\nTens:7.\n\nHundreds:6.\n\nThousands:6.\n\nTen thousands:6.\n\nHundred thousands:4.\n\nPlus the carried over 1 at the million place</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
