 place would be 8 (from first) plus 9 (from second). 8+9=17. So yes, that's 7 in the ten thousands place and carry over 1 to the hundred thousands place.\n\nThen the hundred thousands place: 1 (from first number) + 6 (from second number) plus the carried-over 1 equals 8. So that's 8 in the hundred thousands place.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right: 2 (ones), 8 (tens), 8 (hundreds), 8 (thousands), 7 (ten thousands), and 8 (hundred thousands). Wait, but let me check again step by step to make sure I didn't mix up any digits.\n\nWait, let me write it out vertically:.\n\n      1 8 0 3 7 5.\n    + 6 9 8 5 0 7.\n    ---------------.\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 5 + 7 = 12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 7 + 0 =7 +1=8. Write 8.\n\nHundreds: 3 +5=8. Write 8.\n\nThousands: 0 +8=8. Write 8.\n\nTen thousands: 8 +9=17. Write 7, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands:1 +6=7 +1 (carryover) =8</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
