4 →4, carry1.\n\nHundred thousands:6 +4 =10 +1 (carry) =11 →1, carry1.\n\nThen the million's place: carryover 1.\n\nSo combining all digits: 1 (million), 1 (hundred thousand), 4 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 1 (hundred), 6 (tens), 3 (ones). So 1,146,163. Perfect.\n\nAlright, I think that's solid. The answer is 1,146,163. I'll present this in the template as instructed.\n</think>", '']
