ers with their place values:.\n\n658,388:.\n- Hundred thousands: 6.\n- Ten thousands: 5.\n- Thousands: 8.\n- Hundreds: 3.\n- Tens: 8.\n- Ones: 8.\n\nWait no, actually breaking down:.\n\nWait, 658,388 is:.\nDigits from right:.\nOnes: 8.\nTens: 8.\nHundreds: 3.\nThousands: 8.\nTen thousands:5.\nHundred thousands:6.\n\nSimilarly, 346,038:.\nOnes:8.\nTens:3.\nHundreds:0.\nThousands:6.\nTen thousands:4.\nHundred thousands:3.\n\nSo when adding:.\n\nOnes:8+8=16 (6, carryover1).\nTens:8+3 +1=12 (2, carryover1).\nHundreds:3+0 +1=4 (no carryover).\nThousands:8+6=14 (4, carryover1).\nTen thousands:5+4 +1=10 (0, carryover1).\nHundred thousands:6+3 +1=10 (so 10 here)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
