Starting from the right:.\n\nOnes place:.\n9 (from 670659) + 1 (from 865351) = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nTens place:.\n5 + 5 = 10, plus the 1 carried over is 11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place:.\n6 +3 =9, plus 1 is 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place:.\n0 +5 =5, plus 1 is 6. Write 6, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands place:.\n7 (from first number) +6 (from second number) =13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands place:.\n6 +8 =14, plus the 1 carried over is 15. Write 5 and carryover 1.\n\nMillions place: The carryover 1. Since both numbers don't have millions digits beyond that, so the total is 1,5 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 0 (ones).\n\nWait, so putting all digits together: 1 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 0 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
