rst number) +7 (from second number) = 9. Write 9.\n\nHundred thousands place: 8 +4 =12. So write 2 and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nMillions place: 0 +0 +1 (carry-over) =1.\n\nSo putting it all together:\n\nMillions: 1\n\nHundred thousands:2\n\nTen thousands:9\n\nThousands:7\n\nHundreds:4\n\nTens:8\n\nOnes:8\n\nSo the total is 1,297,488. Wait, so that's the correct answer. But earlier, I had messed up the thousands place by incorrectly taking the second number's thousands digit as 8 instead of 2. So the correct sum is indeed 1,297,488. \n\nLet me verify by another method, like adding the numbers in parts:\n\n825,303 + 472,185.\n\nBreak them into larger chunks. For instance, 800,000 + 400,000 = 1,200,000.\n\nThen 25,303 + 72,185. Let's see:\n\n25,303 +72,185:\n\n25k +72k = 97k, and 303 +185 = 488. So total 97,488.\n\nAdding to the previous 1,200,000 gives 1,297,488. That matches. So the answer is correct.\n\nTherefore, the final sum is 1,297,488.",
