to the millions place. But wait, since there are no digits beyond hundred thousands, that carryover becomes a 1 in the millions place.\n\nPutting it all together: starting from the ones, we had 2, 9, 5, 8, then 0 with a carryover, and then 12 in the hundred thousands. Wait, maybe I need to retrace.\n\nLet me write it out step by step vertically to be sure:.\n\n```.\n  517120.\n+691472.\n--------.\n```.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes place: 0 + 2 = 2.\n\nTens: 2 +7 =9.\n\nHundreds:1 +4=5.\n\nThousands:7 (from 517,120's thousands place) plus 1 (from 691,472's thousands place) = 8.\n\nTen thousands: 1 (from first number) +9 (from second) =10. So write 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands:5 +6 =11, plus the carried 1 makes 12. So 2 in the hundred thousands and carryover 1 to millions.\n\nSo the total sum would have a 1 in the millions place, 2 in hundred thousands, 0 in ten thousands, 8 in thousands, 5 in hundreds, 9 in tens, and 2 in ones</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
