,721 properly.\n\n9,652\n\n+99,721\n\n= ?\n\nAdding units:\n\n2+1=3\n\n5+2=7\n\n6+7=13 (carryover 1)\n\n9+9+1=19 (carryover 1)\n\n0 (since 9,652 has no digit there except leading zeros) +9 (from 99,721's ten thousands place) plus carryover 1 =10. So that would give 109,373? Wait, so then total sum would be 500,000 +109,373 = 609,373. Okay, that matches the previous result. So that's correct. Therefore, the final answer should be 609,373. I think that's right. Maybe I can use another approach: approximate the numbers to check if the answer is reasonable.\n\n109,652 is approximately 110,000 and 499,721 is approximately 500,000. Adding those gives about 610,000. The exact answer is 609,373, which is 627 less than 610,000, which makes sense because we rounded up both numbers by about 348 (110,000 -109,652=348) and 279 (500,000 -499,721=279), so total overestimation was 348+279=627. So the exact answer being 609,373 aligns with that. So that seems correct. Alright, confident now.\n</think>\n\n",
