). Wait, hold on, let me check again because I might have messed up the places. Let me recount each step carefully.\n\nWait, maybe I should write it out more systematically. Let's line them up:.\n\n  887,196.\n+ 930,665.\n----------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 6 + 5 = 11. Write 1, carryover 1. So ones digit is 1.\n\nTens: 9 + 6 = 15 + 1 = 16. Write 6, carryover 1. Tens digit is 6.\n\nHundreds: 1 + 6 = 7 + 1 (carryover) = 8. Hundreds digit is 8, no carryover.\n\nThousands: 7 + 0 = 7. Thousands digit is 7.\n\nTen thousands: 8 (from first number) + 3 (from second) = 11. So here we have 11. Wait, but ten thousands place: the first number has 8 in the ten thousands place (since 887,196 is 8 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands)), yes. The second number is 930,665 which is 9 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands). So adding 8 + 3 = 11. So we write 1 in the ten thousands place and carry over 1 to the hundred thousands.\n\nHundred thousands place: 8 + 9 = 17, plus the carried over 1 makes 18. So write 8 in the hundred thousands and carry over 1 to the millions place. The millions place is just the carried over 1. .\n\nSo putting all the digits together: 1 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 1 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
