ght. But let me add another way to confirm. Maybe adding the numbers as whole:\n\n668,684 + 310,184. Let's break them into parts.\n\n668,684 + 300,000 = 968,684\n\nThen add 10,184: 968,684 +10,000 =978,684, then +184 = 978,868. Yes, that matches. Okay, so the answer is correct. I think that's right. So the final sum is 978,868. \n\nWait, but in my first calculation, when I listed the places, the thousands place was 8 (from first number) plus 0 (second number) gives 8. But in the breakdown, when adding 668,684 +310,184, the thousands digit in the second number is 0? Let me check again:\n\n310,184 is structured as 3 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 4 (ones). So yes, the thousands digit is 0. So adding 8 (from first number) +0 gives 8. Correct. So all steps check out. Therefore, the answer should be 978,868. \n\nI think that's correct. Maybe another way: using expanded form.\n\n668,684 = 600,000 + 60,000 + 8,000 + 600 + 80 +4\n\n310,184 = 300,000 + 10,000 + 0 + 100 +80 +4\n\nAdding each part:\n\n600k +300k =900k\n\n60k +10k=70k\n\n8k +0=8k\n\n600+100=700\n\n80+80=160\n\n4+4=8\n\nNow sum all those:\n\n900,000 +70,000 =970,000\n\n+8,000 =978,000\n\n+700 =978,700\n\n+160 =978,860\n\n+8 =978,868. Perfect, that's the same result. So definitely correct. Alright, confident now.\n</think>\n\n",
