dred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 7 (tens), and 8 (ones). Wait a second, let me check that again because when I added the ten thousands place, I had 8 +1 +1 =10, so that would actually be 0 in that place with a carryover. But then the hundred thousands place was 1+1 plus the carried 1, making 3</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
