housands),3 (thousands),8 (hundreds),1 (tens),8 (ones).\n\nSo when adding the thousands place: the thousands digit in first number is7, second is3. 7+3=10, plus the carryover1 makes 11. So 1 in thousands place, carryover1 to ten thousands.\n\nYes, that's correct. So all steps are consistent. Therefore, the answer is 1,511,504.\n\nI think that's right. I don't see any errors in the calculations now.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 807686 and 703818?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: 6 + 8 = 14. Write down 4 and carry over 1.\n2. The tens place: 8 + 1 = 9 + 1 (carryover) = 10. Write down 0 and carry over 1.\n3. The hundreds place: 6 + 8 = 14 + 1 (carryover) = 15. Write down 5 and carry over 1.\n4. The thousands place: 7 + 3 = 10 + 1 (carryover) = 11. Write down 1 and carry over 1.\n5. The ten thousands place: 0 + 0 + 1 (carryover) = 1.\n6. The hundred thousands place: 8 + 7 = 15. Write down 15.\n\nCombining all the digits: 1,511,504.\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is 1511504.",
