, the hundred thousands place would be 0 with a carryover of 1 to the millions place. But since there are no more digits, that 1 becomes a new digit at the start. So the total would be 1,032,655?.\n\nWait, let me re-add each column step by step again carefully to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nLet me write it out vertically again:.\n\n\u2003\xa0676,936.\n+365,719.\n----------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 6 + 9 = 15 → 5, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 3 + 1 = 4, plus 1 carried over is 5. So 5, no carryover.\n\nHundreds: 9 + 7 = 16 → 6, carryover 1.\n\nThousands: 6 + 5 = 11, plus 1 carried over is 12 → 2, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands: 7 (from 676,936's ten thousands place? Wait, let me confirm the digits:.\n\nWait, let's break down each number digit by digit:.\n\nFirst number: 676,936.\n\nDigits from right to left (ones to hundred thousands):.\n\nPosition: Ones: 6.\n\nTens: 3.\n\nHundreds: 9.\n\nThousands: 6.\n\nTen thousands: 7.\n\nHundred thousands: 6.\n\nSecond number: 365,719.\n\nDigits from right to left:.\n\nOnes:9.\n\nTens:1.\n\nHundreds:7.\n\nThousands:5.\n\nTen thousands:6.\n\nHundred thousands:3.\n\nSo when adding:.\n\nOnes: 6 +9 =15.\n\nTens:3+1=4 +1=5.\n\nHundreds:9+7=16 →6, carryover 1.\n\nThousands:6 (from first) +5 (second) =11, plus 1 is 12 →2, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:7 (first) +6 (second)=13, plus 1 →14 →4, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:6 +3=9 plus 1 →10 →0 with carryover1.\n\nThen the million place: the carried over 1</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
