final_output:  ['1,356,284.\n\nWait, let me check again. Maybe I made a mistake in the places. Let me add them step by step again.\n\nBreaking down each digit:\n\nFirst number: 560,284 is:\n\n- Hundred thousands: 5\n\n- Ten thousands:6\n\n- Thousands:0\n\n- Hundreds:2\n\n- Tens:8\n\n- Ones:4\n\nSecond number:796,000 is:\n\n- Hundred thousands:7\n\n- Ten thousands:9\n\n- Thousands:6\n\n- Hundreds:0\n\n- Tens:0\n\n- Ones:0\n\nAdding each place:\n\nOnes: 4+0=4\n\nTens:8+0=8\n\nHundreds:2+0=2\n\nThousands:0+6=6\n\nTen thousands:6 +9=15 → write 5, carryover 1\n\nHundred thousands:5 +7=12, plus the carried over 1 makes 13 → so write 3 in hundred thousands and carryover 1 to millions.\n\nMillions place: 1 (from carryover). \n\nSo combining all, the digits are:\n\nMillions:1, Hundred thousands:3, Ten thousands:5, Thousands:6, Hundreds:2, Tens:8, Ones:4 → 1,356,284. That seems right. So the answer should be correct.\n\nWait another way to check: Maybe adding the numbers as whole numbers.\n\n560,284 + 796,000.\n\nLet me add 560,000 + 796,000 = 1,356,000. Then add the remaining 284: 1,356,000 + 284 = 1,356,284. Yep, same result. Okay, that confirms it. So the final answer is 1,356,284.', '']
