ee! In my first vertical calculation, I thought that the thousands place was 1 (from first number) +7 (from second number). Wait, let me check the thousands digit again.\n\nWait, the first number is 141,967:\n\nBreaking down:\n\n1 (hundred thousand)\n\n4 (ten thousand)\n\n1 (thousand)\n\n9 (hundred)\n\n6 (ten)\n\n7 (one)\n\nSecond number: 297,050:\n\n2 (hundred thousand)\n\n9 (ten thousand)\n\n7 (thousand)\n\n0 (hundred)\n\n5 (ten)\n\n0 (one)\n\nSo, the thousands place: the first number has a 1 (in the thousands place), and the second number has a 7 (in the thousands place). So adding those gives 1 +7 =8, plus the carryover from the hundreds place (which was 1) \u2192 8+1=9. So that's correct.\n\nSo thousands digit is 9.\n\nTen thousands place: 4 +9 =13, so 3 with a carryover. So ten thousands is 3, carryover 1 to hundred thousands.\n\nHundred thousands:1 +2 =3 plus the carryover 1 =4.\n\nSo the digits are 4 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 1 (tens),7 (ones). So the number is 439,017. So my first calculation was wrong because I must have miscalculated the ten thousands place.\n\nWait, so in my first reasoning, I wrote:\n\n\"Ten thousands place:4 +9 =13. So write 3, carryover 1 to the hundred thousands.\"\n\nThen hundred thousands:1 +2 +1=4. So the digits would be 4 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands)... So that's 439,017, not 438,017. I must have made a typo in my initial thought. So the correct answer is 439,017.\n\nTherefore, my first vertical calculation was wrong because I probably miscalculated the ten thousands place. The second method gave 439,017, which matches the corrected vertical addition. So the correct answer is 439,017.\n\nI need to be careful with the places. Let me confirm with another method: using calculator-like addition.\n\n141,967 + 297,050.\n\nAdding 141,967 + 297,050:\n\nLet me add 141,967 + 297,050:\n\nStart with 141,967 + 200,000 = 341,967.\n\nThen add 97,050:\n\n341,967 + 97,050:\n\n341,967 + 90,000 = 431,967.\n\n431,967 + 7,050 = 439,017. Yes, that matches. So the correct answer is 439,017.\n\nTherefore, in my initial reasoning I must have made a mistake in the digit places. Probably mixed up the thousands and ten thousands.\n\nAlright, so the correct answer is 439,017. I need to adjust the reasoning accordingly.\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: 7 + 0 = 7\n2. The tens place: 6 + 5 = 11. Write down 1 and carry over 1.\n3. The hundreds place: 9 + 0 + 1 (carryover) = 10. Write down 0 and carry over 1.\n4. The thousands place: 1 + 7 + 1 (carryover) = 9. Write down 9.\n5. The ten thousands place: 4 + 9 = 13. Write down 3 and carry over 1.\n6. The hundred thousands place: 1 + 2 + 1 (carryover) = 4.\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is 439017.",
