ndred thousands place).\n\nWait, here's where I might have made a mistake earlier. The ten thousands place addition: 6 (from first number) + 9 (from second number) equals 15. So that would be 5 in the ten thousands place and carry over 1 to the hundred thousands place. .\n\nThen the hundred thousands place: 9 + 3 is 12, plus the carried over 1 makes 13. So that would be 3 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place. .\n\nSo putting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right, the digits are:.\n\nOnes:5, Tens:6, Hundreds:5, Thousands:9, Ten thousands:5 (with a carryover 1), Hundred thousands:3 (with a carryover 1), and then the million's place is that 1 carried over</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
