't mix up the places. Maybe I should write each digit's place explicitly.\n\nLet me list each digit position:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes place:.\nFirst number: 7.\nSecond number: 6.\nTotal: 7 + 6 = 13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nTens place:.\nFirst number: 5.\nSecond number: 3.\nPlus carryover 1: 5 + 3 + 1 = 9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nHundreds place:.\nFirst number: 8.\nSecond number: 9.\nTotal: 8 + 9 = 17. Write 7, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place:.\nFirst number: 4.\nSecond number: 4.\nPlus carryover 1: 4 + 4 + 1 = 9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nTen-thousands place:.\nFirst number: 0.\nSecond number: 9.\nTotal: 0 + 9 = 9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nHundred-thousands place:.\nFirst number: 2.\nSecond number: 2.\nTotal: 2 + 2 = 4. Write 4</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
