he hundred thousands? Wait, no, the hundred thousands place addition is separate. Wait, let me go step by step again.\n\nLet me do the addition step by step again carefully:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):.\n\nOnes place:.\n0 + 8 = 8. Write down 8.\n\nTens place:.\n6 + 9 = 15. Write down 5, carryover 1 to the hundreds.\n\nHundreds place:.\n4 + 7 = 11, plus the carried 1 is 12. Write down 2, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place:.\n2 (from first number) + 0 (from second number) = 2, plus the carried 1 = 3. Write down 3. No carryover here.\n\nTen thousands place:.\n3 (from first number) + 0 (from second number) = 3. Write down 3. No carryover.\n\nHundred thousands place:.\n3 (from first number) + 9 (from second number) = 12. Write down 12.\n\nSo putting all the digits together, starting from the right:.\n\nOnes:8, Tens:5, Hundreds:2, Thousands:3, Ten thousands:3, Hundred thousands:12.\n\nWait, but writing it out, the hundred thousands place is 12, so the total number would be 12 followed by the other digits</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
