ds: 2.\n- Tens: 6.\n- Ones: 1.\n\n512,719 is:.\n- Hundred thousands: 5.\n- Ten thousands: 1.\n- Thousands: 2.\n- Hundreds: 7.\n- Tens: 1.\n- Ones: 9.\n\nAdding each column from right to left:.\n\nOnes place: 1 + 9 = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nTens place: 6 + 1 = 7, plus the carryover 1 makes 8. Write 8, no carryover.\n\nHundreds place: 2 +7 =9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nThousands place: 6 +2 =8. Wait, original numbers: first number's thousands place is 6 (since 706,261: the digits are 7,0,6,2,6,1). Wait, maybe I miscounted the places. Let me check again.\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the thousands place. Let me write both numbers with their place values clearly:.\n\nLet me write 706261 as:.\n\nDigit positions (from right):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 1.\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 6.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds): 2.\n\nPosition 4 (thousands): 6.\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands): 0.\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):7.\n\nSimilarly, 512719:.\n\nPosition 1:9.\n\nPosition 2:1.\n\nPosition3:7.\n\nPosition4:2.\n\nPosition5:1.\n\nPosition6:5.\n\nSo adding each position:.\n\nPosition1: 1+9=10 → 0 carryover 1.\n\nPosition2:6+1=7 +1=8 → 8, no carryover.\n\nPosition3:2+7=9 →9.\n\nPosition4:6 (from first) +2 (from second) =8 →8.\n\nPosition5:0 +1 =1 →1.\n\nPosition6:7 +5=12 → 2, carryover 1.\n\nNow, the carryover from position6 (hundred thousands) is 1, so we add a new digit at the millions place:1.\n\nPutting all together from right to left:.\n\nThe digits are:.\n\nMillions:1.\n\nHundred thousands:2.\n\nTen thousands:1.\n\nThousands:8.\n\nHundreds:9.\n\nTens:8.\n\nOnes:0</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
