y:.\n\n403858.\n+122533.\n--------.\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 8 + 3 = 11. Write down 1, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 5 + 3 = 8 + 1 = 9. Write 9.\n\nHundreds: 8 + 5 = 13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nThousands: 3 (from 403858) + 2 (from 122533) = 5 + 1 (carryover) = 6. Wait, the thousands digit in the first number is 3? Let me check the original numbers again. .\n\nWait, 403,858 is broken down as:.\n\nDigits (from right): 8 (ones), 5 (tens), 8 (hundreds), 3 (thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 4 (hundred thousands).\n\nThe second number, 122,533 is:.\n\n3 (ones), 3 (tens), 5 (hundreds), 2 (thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 1 (hundred thousands).\n\nSo when adding the thousands place: 3 (from first number) + 2 (from second) = 5, plus the carryover 1 from the hundreds place (which was 13, so carryover 1). So 5 +1 =6. So thousands digit is 6. No carryover.\n\nThen the ten thousands place: 0 (from first number) + 2 (from second) = 2. .\n\nHundred thousands place: 4 +1 =5.\n\nSo putting all together, the digits from right to left are:.\n\nOnes:1, Tens:9, Hundreds:3, Thousands:6, Ten thousands:2, Hundred thousands:5</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
