(ones).\n\nYes, so thousands place is 9. The second number, 734,382:.\n\n7 (hundred thousands).\n3 (ten thousands).\n4 (thousands).\n3 (hundreds).\n8 (tens).\n2 (ones).\n\nSo thousands place is 4. So adding 9 + 4 = 13. So thousands place is 3, carryover 1.\n\nMoving to ten thousands place: 8 (from first number) + 3 (from second) + 1 (carryover) = 12. So ten thousands place is 2, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands place: 3 + 7 + 1 (carryover) = 11. So that's 1 in the hundred thousands place and carryover 1 to the millions place. Wait, but since both numbers only have up to hundred thousands, the carryover would make a new digit in the millions</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
