 second has 0. 0 + 0 = 0.\n\nHundred thousands place: first has 9, second has 1. 9 + 1 = 10.\n\nWait, putting all together:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 11 → 1, carry 1.\n\nTens: 2+0+1=3.\n\nHundreds:4+2=6.\n\nThousands:4+2=6.\n\nTen thousands:0+0=0.\n\nHundred thousands:9+1=10</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
