hundreds place: 7 (from first) + 7 (from second) = 14, plus the carried over 1 makes 15. So we write 5 and carry over 1 again.\n\nThousands place: 0 (from first number) + 6 (from second) = 6, plus the carried over 1 is 7. So thousands digit is 7, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands place: 1 (from first number) + 2 (from second) = 3. No carryover here.\n\nHundred thousands place: 4 (from first) + 2 (from second) = 6.\n\nPutting all together: 6 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 9 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
