 + 8 = 14.\n\nWait, let me go through each step again carefully to avoid mistakes.\n\nStarting over:.\n\nOnes place:.\n9 (from 631,799) + 4 (from 844,744) = 13. So, ones digit is 3, carryover 1.\n\nTens place:.\n9 (tens of first number) + 4 (tens of second number) = 13, plus the carried 1 makes 14. So tens digit is 4, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place:.\n7 (hundreds of first) +7 (hundreds of second) =14, plus 1 carried =15. So hundreds digit 5, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place:.\n1 (thousands of first) +4 (thousands of second) =5, plus 1 carried makes 6. So thousands digit 6, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands place:.\n3 (ten thousands of first) +4 (ten thousands of second) =7. So ten thousands digit is 7.\n\nHundred thousands place:.\n6 (hundred thousands of first) +8 (hundred thousands of second) =14. So that's 4 in the hundred thousands place and carryover 1 to the millions place. Wait, but since both numbers are up to hundred thousands, adding them gives a possible million. So the total would be 14 in the hundred thousands, which is actually 1,400,000. So that would mean writing 4 in the hundred thousands and carrying 1 to the millions place. Since there's no higher digits, the total becomes 1,4</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
