lace. Wait, but how do we write that? Since each place can only hold a single digit, the 14 here would mean 4 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place. But since both original numbers are six-digit, adding them might result in a seven-digit number. So adding the hundred thousands: 8 +6 =14. So we write 4 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place. Therefore, the millions place will have that 1.\n\nPutting it all together: starting from the right, the digits we have are:.\n\nOnes: 2.\n\nTens:7.\n\nHundreds:7.\n\nThousands:0.\n\nTen thousands:8.\n\nHundred thousands:4.\n\nMillions:1</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
