t step by step carefully.\n\nStarting over:.\n\nNumber1: 642,022.\nNumber2: 528,831.\n\nBreaking down each digit:.\n\nLet's write them aligned properly:.\n\n\u2003\u20036 4 2 0 2 2.\n+\u20035 2 8 8 3 1.\n------------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\n1. Ones place: 2 + 1 = 3. Write down 3.\n2. Tens place: 2 + 3 = 5. Write down 5.\n3. Hundreds place: 0 + 8 = 8. Write down 8.\n4. Thousands place: 2 + 8 = 10. Write down 0, carry over 1.\n5. Ten thousands place: 4 + 2 = 6, plus the carried 1 makes 7. Write down 7.\n6. Hundred thousands place: 6 + 5 = 11. Since there's no more digits, write 11.\n\nPutting it all together: 11 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 3 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
