re no more digits, that carried-over 1 becomes a 1 in the millions place.\n\nPutting it all together: starting from the right, the digits are 7 (ones), 4 (tens), 0 (hundreds), 7 (thousands), 6 (ten-thousands), 0 (hundred-thousands), and the carried-over 1 in the millions</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
