re now 7 digits: the carried 1 in millions, then 0 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 7 (ones). So the number is 1,067,047.\n\nWait, but let me check with another method. Maybe adding the numbers as whole numbers:\n\n900,875 + 166,172.\n\nLet me break them into parts:\n\n900,000 + 875\n\n+166,000 + 172\n\nAdding the thousands: 900,000 + 166,000 = 1,066,000\n\nAdding the remaining: 875 +172 = 1,047\n\nSo total is 1,066,000 + 1,047 = 1,067,047. Yes, that matches. So the answer should be 1,067,047.\n\nSo the reasoning steps would be:\n\n1. Ones place: 5 + 2 = 7\n\n2. Tens place:7 +7=14, carryover 1\n\n3. Hundreds place:8 +1 +1=10, write 0 carryover 1\n\n4. Thousands place:0 +6 +1=7\n\n5. Ten-thousands place:0 +6=6\n\n6. Hundred-thousands place:9 +1=10, so write 0 and carryover 1 to millions place.\n\nThus the final sum is 1,067,047.\n\nI think that's correct. Let me just add them directly:\n\n900,875\n\n+166,172\n\nAdding:\n\nStart from the right:\n\n5+2=7\n\n70+70=140, so 4 in tens, carry 1.\n\n800 + 100 = 900, plus 100 (carry) is 1000. So 0 in hundreds, carry 1.\n\n0 (thousands place from first number) +6 (thousands from second) is 6, plus the carried 1 makes 7.\n\n0 (ten thousands) +6 (ten thousands) =6.\n\n9 (hundred thousands) +1 (hundred thousands) =10, so that's 10 in that place, which is written as 0 with a carryover to millions.\n\nSo the total is 1,067,047. Yep, same result. Okay, confident now.\n</think>\n\n",
