ng it all together, starting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 2.\n\nTens: 4 (with a carryover).\n\nHundreds: 5 (with a carryover).\n\nThousands: 9.\n\nTen-thousands: 9.\n\nHundred-thousands: 4 (plus the carryover from the hundred-thousands addition).\n\nAnd then the new millions digit from the carryover: 1</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
