ave messed up the positions.\n\nWait, let me write it step by step properly:.\n\nLet me align them properly:.\n\n      1 3 4 0 3 5.\n    + 9 8 2 6 3 3.\n    ----------------.\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes place: 5 + 3 = 8. Write down 8.\n\nTens: 3 + 3 = 6. Write 6.\n\nHundreds: 0 + 6 = 6. Write 6.\n\nThousands: 4 + 2 = 6. Write 6.\n\nTen-thousands: 3 + 8 = 11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nHundred-thousands: 1 + 9 = 10, plus the carried 1 is 11. So write 1 here and carryover 1.\n\nSince there's a carryover, we add a new digit at the millions place: 1.\n\nSo putting all together, the sum is 1 (million), 1 (hundred-thousands), 1 (ten-thousands), 6 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 8 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
