ait, let me check that again. Let me add step by step:.\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the places. Let me write each digit position clearly.\n\nLet me line up the numbers:.\n\n      834430.\n    + 185991.\n    -----------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 0 + 1 = 1  .\nTens: 3 + 9 = 12 (write 2, carry 1)  .\nHundreds: 4 + 9 + 1 (carry) = 14 (write 4, carry 1)  .\nThousands: 4 + 5 +1 (carry) = 10 (write 0, carry 1)  .\nTen-thousands: 3 + 8 +1 (carry) = 12 (write 2, carry 1)  .\nHundred-thousands: 8 + 1 +1 (carry) = 10 (write 0, carry 1)  .\nMillions: the carryover 1</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
