ee:.\n\nBreaking down both numbers:.\n\n975,909:.\n- Millions: 0 (since it's a 6-digit number).\n- Hundred thousands:9.\n- Ten thousands:7.\n- Thousands:5.\n- Hundreds:9.\n- Tens:0.\n- Ones:9.\n\n373,045:.\n- Hundred thousands:3.\n- Ten thousands:7.\n- Thousands:3.\n- Hundreds:0.\n- Tens:4.\n- Ones:5.\n\nWait, so aligning each digit properly:.\n\nHundred thousands place: 9 +3 =12.\n\nTen thousands:7 +7 =14.\n\nThousands place:5 +3 =8.\n\nHundreds place:9 +0 =9.\n\nTens:0 +4=4.\n\nOnes:9 +5=14.\n\nWait, so actually starting from the right, the places are:.\n\nOnes:9+5=14 → 4, carryover 1.\n\nTens:0+4=4 +1=5 → no carryover.\n\nHundreds:9+0=9.\n\nThousands:5 +3=8.\n\nTen thousands:7 +7=14 → write 4, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands:9 +3=12 +1 (carryover) =13 → write 3, carryover 1.\n\nMillions place: 0 +0 +1 (carryover) =1.\n\nSo putting it all together:.\n\nMillions:1, Hundred thousands:3, Ten thousands:4, thousands:8, hundreds:9, tens:5, ones:4</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
