), and the carried-over 1 at the hundred thousands place makes it a 7 in the millions place. Wait, let me check that again. Wait, the hundred thousands place digits were 7 and 9. 7+9=16, so actually, the hundred thousands place would be 6, and carryover 1 to the millions place. Since both original numbers are six-digit numbers, adding them can give a seven-digit number</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
