\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 6 +8 =14 → 4, carry 1.\n\nTens:6+8+1=15 →5, carry1.\n\nHundreds:0+4+1=5 →5, no carry.\n\nThousands:8+7=15 →5, carry1.\n\nTen thousands:0+0+1=1.\n\nHundred thousands:5+7=12 →2, carry 1.\n\nMillions place: the carried over 1.\n\nSo putting all together:\n\nMillions:1, hundred thousands:2, ten thousands:1, thousands:5, hundreds:5, tens:5, ones:4.\n\nSo the number is 1,215,554. That seems right. Let me add them using another method to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, adding 508,066 +707,488.\n\nBreak them into parts:\n\n500,000 + 700,000 =1,200,000.\n\n8,066 +7,488 = ?\n\n8,000 +7,000 =15,000.\n\n66 +488 = 554.\n\nSo total of those parts:15,000+554=15,554.\n\nThen total sum:1,200,000 +15,554=1,215,554. Yep, same result. Okay, so that must be correct.\n\nSo the answer is 1,215,554.\n\n</think>", '']
