t, hold on, let me check again step by step because I might have messed up the places.\n\nWait, maybe I should do it step by step vertically. Let me try again:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes column: 7 + 9 = 16. So 6, carryover 1.\n\nTens column: 2 + 8 = 10, plus 1 is 11. So 1, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds column: 7 + 9 = 16, plus 1 is 17. So 7, carryover 1.\n\nThousands column: 2 (from first number) +1 (from second number) = 3, plus 1 carried over is 4. So 4, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands column: 1 (from first number) +5 (from second) = 6. So 6, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands column: 5 +8 =13. So 3 in the hundred thousands place and carryover 1 to millions place. Wait, but 5+8 is 13, so actually, the hundred thousands place becomes 3 and we have a 1 in the millions place. .\n\nSo putting it all together, the total sum is 1 (millions) 3 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 6 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
