ct that. This is a common mistake when adding. Let me start over step by step properly.\n\nLet me align both numbers vertically:\n\n      4 0 5 3 6 1\n    + 3 4 6 6 1 4\n    ----------------\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):\n\nOnes: 1 + 4 = 5. Write down 5.\n\nTens: 6 + 1 =7. Write 7.\n\nHundreds: 3 +6 =9. Write 9.\n\nThousands place: 5 (from first number) +6 (from second number) = 11. Here, we write down 1 and carry over 1 to the next (ten-thousands) column.\n\nTen-thousands place: 0 (from first number) +4 (second number) plus the carried over 1. So 0+4=4, plus 1 is 5. So write 5 here.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 4 +3 =7. Since there's no carryover from the previous step (the ten-thousands place only had a carried over 1 which was added there), so 4+3=7. Write that down.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum would be 7 (hundred-thousands), 5 (ten-thousands), 1 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 5 (ones). Wait, but when we had the thousands place, we had 11, so we write 1 and carry over 1. So the thousands digit is 1, and the ten-thousands becomes 5 (0+4+1). So the total is 751,975?\n\nWait, let me write it out step by step with the carryover:\n\nLet me write each digit step by step with the carry:\n\nPositions (from right):\n\n1. Ones: 1+4=5. No carry.\n2. Tens:6+1=7. No carry.\n3. Hundreds:3+6=9. No carry.\n4. Thousands:5+6=11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n5. Ten-thousands:0+4 +1 (carry) =5. No carry.\n6. Hundred-thousands:4+3=7. No carry.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nHundred-thousands:7\n\nTen-thousands:5\n\nThousands:1\n\nHundreds:9\n\nTens:7\n\nOnes:5\n\nTherefore, the number is 751,975. Wait, but when I first did it without considering the carryover, I thought I had 769,975, but that was wrong because I miscalculated the thousands place. So the correct answer is 751,975?\n\nWait but let me verify with another method. Let's add the numbers another way to check.\n\n405,361 + 346,614.\n\nLet me break them into parts:\n\n400,000 + 5,000 + 300 + 60 +1\n\nplus\n\n30