 the right:.\n\nOnes: 0 + 9 = 9.\n\nTens: 9 + 0 = 9.\n\nHundreds: 6 + 5 = 11. Write down 1, carryover 1.\n\nThousands: 3 (from first number) + 1 (from second) plus the carryover 1 makes 5. So 5.\n\nTen thousands: 0 (from first) + 1 (from second) = 1.\n\nHundred thousands: 1 (from first) + 8 (from second) = 9.\n\nSo combining all digits: 9 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 9 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
