as a discrepancy. So all methods give 800,988. That's reassuring.\n\nTherefore, the sum is 800,988. I think that's correct. The key was making sure the carries were handled properly, especially in the ten thousands place where another carryover occurred. The initial step-by-step digit addition and the breakdown method both confirm the same result. I don't see any errors now. So the final answer is 800,988.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 409828 and 391160 is \\boxed{800988}.\n</think>\n\n",
