t all together:\n\n1 (million), 4 (hundred thousand), 5 (ten thousand), 6 (thousand), 9 (hundred),7 (ten),8 (one). So 1,456,978. Yep, that's correct.\n\nI think that's right. Let me check with another method, like column addition written out:\n\n\u202f\u00a0683484\n\n+773494\n\n----------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 4+4=8\n\nTens:8+9=17 (write 7, carry 1)\n\nHundreds:4+4=8 +1=9\n\nThousands:3+3=6\n\nTen-thousands:8+7=15 (write 5, carry 1)\n\nHundred-thousands:6+7=13 +1=14 (so 4, carry 1)\n\nMillions: 1.\n\nSo combining all digits: 1,4 (hundred thousands),5 (ten thousands),6 (thousands),9 (hundreds),7 (tens),8 (ones). Yep, 1,456,978.\n\nAlright, confident that's correct.\n</think>\n\n",
