digit by digit properly. Let me write both numbers with commas to clarify:.\n\n816,610 is 8 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 0 (ones).\n\n699,172 is 6 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 2 (ones).\n\nSo aligning them:.\n\n      8 1 6 6 1 0.\n    + 6 9 9 1 7 2.\n    ----------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):.\n\n0 + 2 = 2 (ones place).\n\nTens place: 1 + 7 = 8 (tens place).\n\nHundreds place: 6 + 1 = 7 (hundreds place).\n\nThousands place: 6 (from first number) + 9 (from second) = 15. Wait, here's a mistake earlier. Wait, thousands place in first number is the fourth digit from the right. Let me recount:.\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the digit places. Let me list each digit position clearly:.\n\nNumber1: 816,610.\n\nBreaking down each digit from right to left (ones to hundred thousands):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 0.\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 1.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds): 6.\n\nPosition 4 (thousands): 6.\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands): 1.\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands): 8.\n\nNumber2: 699,172.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 2.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):7.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):1.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):9.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):9.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):6.\n\nSo adding each column:.\n\nPosition 1: 0 +2=2.\n\nPosition2:1+7=8.\n\nPosition3:6+1=7.\n\nPosition4:6 +9=15. So write down 5, carryover 1.\n\nPosition5:1 (from first number) +9 (from second) +1 (carryover)=11. So write 1, carryover 1.\n\nPosition6:8 +6 +1 (carryover) =15. So here, the hundred thousands place sum is 15. But since there are no higher digits, we need to write 15 as 5 in the hundred thousands and carryover 1 to a new million's place. Wait, so the total becomes 1 (million) 5 (hundred thousand) .. etc. .\n\nSo putting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right, the digits are 2,8,7,5 (with carryover), then position5 gives 1 (with carryover), position6 gives 15, which with the carryover becomes 15+1? Wait, maybe I need to track the carryover again step by step.\n\nLet me go through each step again carefully:.\n\nAdding the numbers:.\n\nPositions:.\n\n1 (ones): 0 +2 =2. No carryover.\n\n2 (tens):1 +7=8. No carryover.\n\n3 (hundreds):6+1=7. No carryover.\n\n4 (thousands):6+9=15. Write down 5, carryover 1.\n\n5 (ten thousands):1 (from first number) +9 (second) +1 (carryover)=11. So write down 1, carryover 1.\n\n6 (hundred thousands):8 +6 +1 (carryover)=15. So write down 5, and carryover 1 to the millions place.\n\nSince there are no more digits, that carryover 1 becomes the millions digit.\n\nSo the total digits from right to left are:.\n\nPosition1:2.\n\nPosition2:8.\n\nPosition3:7.\n\nPosition4:5.\n\nPosition5:1.\n\nPosition6:5.\n\nPlus the carried over 1 in the millions place (position7).\n\nSo the sum is 1 (million) 5 (hundred thousand) 1 (ten thousand) 5 (thousand) 7 (hundred) 8 (tens) 2 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
